    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily into matchup favorable splits, headlined by **Brady House** and **Nasim Nunez**, who boast the strongest daily efficiency scores of 63.81 and 62.09, respectively. Both benefit significantly from a positive park factor and a exploitable matchup against Woods Richardson (4.85 xERA), with **Brady House** in particular seeing his floor elevated by a +9% dynamic platoon advantage. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a lineup lock with a 69.76 score; despite a neutral matchup against Meyer, **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s aggressive order placement at leadoff and a strong +14% dynamic platoon adjustment underscore his status as our primary engine today. While **Liam Hicks** and **Jacob Wilson** operate in the marginal tier, their involvement is necessary to maintain depth against current SP rotations.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Coby Mayo**, who finished with a 38.03, falling just shy of our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor.\" While **Coby Mayo** offers high-ceiling potential, the combined drag of a suboptimal #8 batting position and the matchup against Meyer\u2019s 3.69 xERA neutralized his projected offensive impact. We are carefully monitoring the health of our core; while we remain without the services of **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** due to scheduling and IL stints, our depth\u2014including **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Marcell Ozuna**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Dominic Smith**\u2014remains under review for upcoming shifts in series pitching assignments. No immediate weather-related risks are flagged, but we are keeping a close eye on **Liam Hicks** as the lone defensive anchor in a matchup against Povich (L), where his left-on-left disadvantage remains a slight concern for his efficiency.",
